#### 4. Authoritative Factual Sources
* **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS):** Mandatory 3-mark hallmarking framework (BIS triangular standard mark, purity/fineness mark such as 22K916, 18K750, 14K585, and 6-digit alphanumeric HUID) verifiable via the official BIS CARE app. Exclusively applicable to solid precious metals; micro-plated items cannot be hallmarked.
* **Ministry of Consumer Affairs & Legal Metrology:** Hallmarking and consumer disclosure mandates regarding base metal versus precious metal definitions.
* **GST Council of India:** 3% composite retail GST applicable to authentic precious metal jewellery and bullion.
* **World Gold Council / Gemological Standards:** Precious metal density, metallurgy, plating durability (microns and electrophoretic lacquer), and melting liquidity.

